## Findings

### F1. HIGH. The 6-second status poll downloads the whole 31.8 MB project every time
- Code: `src/components/assets/AssetsWorkspaceView.jsx:152-156` (`setInterval(bridge.status, 1500*4)`),
  served by `scripts/AssetsService.mjs:1335` -> `snapshot()` 434-465 which ships every file plus `mapping`.
- Trigger: any project open while the Mac bridge is connected, forever.
- MEASURED: 31,794,094 bytes per poll for vegetation; 94 ms service CPU; 27 to 34 ms parse in the
  page; 5.3 MB/s sustained. Command: `node scratch-frontend/snapshot-size.mjs scratch-frontend vegetation-assets-collection-01`.
- Fix: split `status` into a light reply (`sync`, `jobs`, `workspace`, `inventory.count`, plus a
  `filesRevision` counter bumped by inventory/archive/restore) and fetch `files` only when the
  revision differs (or a delta since revision). Strip server-only fields from the client copy
  (manifestPath, relativeManifest, expectedCloudPath, sourceFolder, changeToken, ctimeMs): the cloud
  snapshot at AssetsService.mjs:466-471 already proves a trimmed shape is acceptable to the UI.

### F2. HIGH. A running job polls the same 31.8 MB status every 1.5 s
- Code: `AssetsWorkspaceView.jsx:186-195` (`while` loop, `bridge.status` then `setTimeout(SETTINGS.pollMs)`),
  on top of the 6 s interval of F1.
- Trigger: every archive, restore, unload, recover, prepare-scene launched from the page. A
  vegetation archive can last minutes to an hour (jobTimeoutMs 3,600,000).
- MEASURED basis: 31.8 MB and 94 ms per call (F1) => about 21 MB/s and about 6 % of one service
  core during the whole job, plus a 27 ms parse and a full re-render pipeline (F3) every 1.5 s in
  the page. Impact during the job ESTIMATED from those measured unit costs.
- Fix: a `job` action returning only `{ id, state, progress, count, error }` for `response.jobId`,
  polled at 1.5 s; refresh files once on `done`.

### F3. HIGH. Each status reply rebuilds every project and re-sorts 18,423 files with a slow comparator
- Code: `AssetsWorkspaceView.jsx:154` replaces the `local` array even when nothing changed ->
  `projects` memo 146-149 recomputes `mergeWorkspaceProjects` for all projects and spreads
  `{...file, projectId}` over 38,165 files -> `ProjectWorkspace.jsx:239` `files` memo (fileView) ->
  248-251 `visible` = `queryAssetsFiles` -> `src/lib/assetsFileQuery.js:44-50` sorts with
  `String.localeCompare(b, 'fr', { numeric, sensitivity })`, which builds an Intl collator per call;
  plus `StorageBreakdown` 12, `FileFilters` 8-9 recompute.
- MEASURED (pipeline-timing.mjs, 154,000 index paths, vegetation active):
  mergeWorkspaceProjects 81.7 ms; fileView 9.2 ms; queryAssetsFiles default name sort 336.4 ms
  (same sort with one hoisted `Intl.Collator`: 20.2 ms); storageBreakdown 8.9 ms; FileFilters 4.0 ms.
  Total about 440 ms of main-thread work every 6 s (every 1.5 s during a job). Sort by kind 173 ms.
- Fix: (a) hoist `const collator = new Intl.Collator('fr', { numeric: true, sensitivity: 'base' })`
  in assetsFileQuery.js and use `collator.compare` (17x faster, same order); (b) in the status
  handler keep the previous object when `checkedAt` and the files revision are unchanged, so no memo
  invalidates; (c) see F4 for the index scan.

### F4. MEDIUM. mergeWorkspaceProjects scans the whole search index once per project on every recompute
- Code: `src/lib/assetsWorkspaceViewModel.js:9` and 24/28 call `projectPaths(folder, paths)`,
  `src/lib/assetsProjects.js:91-95` = `paths.filter(startsWith)` over the full index for each
  workspace and each linked legacy collection.
- MEASURED: merge = 14.4 ms with an empty index, 81.7 ms at 154,000 paths, 172.5 ms at 400,000
  (`node scratch-frontend/pipeline-timing.mjs scratch-frontend <N>`), i.e. about 67 ms of pure
  index scanning per recompute, growing linearly with the drive.
- Fix: build `Map<folder, path[]>` once per `paths` reference (WeakMap cache keyed by the array, or
  one pass grouping by the `pages/ZenRayAssets/<project>/` prefix) and let `cloudWorkspaceFiles`
  look it up; status polls then never touch the index.

### F5. MEDIUM. File search matches every file on common letters and costs 324 ms per keystroke
- Code: `src/lib/assetsFileQuery.js:34` builds the haystack from name + relativePath + localPath +
  cloudPath + expectedCloudPath and lowercases it per file per keystroke; `ProjectWorkspace.jsx:79`
  already precomputes `file.searchable` but nothing reads it; no debounce on the input (342).
- MEASURED (vegetation, 18,423 files): "a" matches 18,423 files (every local path contains
  `/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-vegetation-assets-collection-01/`), 324 ms; "pl" 1,099 matches,
  47 ms; "plant" 0 matches, 15 ms. So "tmp", "zenray", "vegetation", "a", "e" filter nothing.
- Fix: search `file.searchable` built from name + relativePath (paths relative to the source,
  not the absolute root), and wrap the query in `useDeferredValue` (or a 150 ms debounce); with F3a
  the full-match case drops to about 20 ms.

### F6. MEDIUM. Viewing a project triggers a full disk inventory and two whole-registry payloads
- Code: `AssetsWorkspaceView.jsx:159-167` calls `bridge.inventory(workspace.id)` on every project
  selection and on every `refreshKey` bump; `refresh()` 117-137 calls `bridge.list()` on mount,
  after every finished job (192), on watch toggle (235), on link (254) and on the Retry button.
  `AssetsService.mjs:294-354` inventory rescans all sources, rewrites the state file, rebuilds the
  global context index, schedules scene audits and returns the full snapshot; `list` 1321-1325
  returns every project's full snapshot.
- MEASURED: list = 64.3 MB (all 15 projects, 38,165 files); inventory reply 31.8 MB plus a 31 MB
  state rewrite (Project-vegetation...json is 32,487,495 bytes) and the 2.1 MB GlobalProjectIndex.
  Opening the vegetation page therefore moves about 96 MB of JSON before the first status poll.
  Rescan duration not measured (would mutate state): ESTIMATED seconds for 18,243 files.
- Fix: the page must not cause writes. Use `status` on selection (the watcher already keeps the
  inventory current), make `list` return summaries (id, name, category, cover, sync, counts) without
  `files`, and keep `inventory` behind the explicit "Actualiser les états" button only.

### F7. MEDIUM. One transient status failure disconnects the page and starts a 64 MB reconnect loop
- Code: `AssetsWorkspaceView.jsx:154` `.catch(() => setConnected(false))`; 139-143 then calls
  `bridge.list()` every 15 s until it answers; 144 swaps conversations to the cloud copy; the status
  `setInterval` has no in-flight guard while each request may take up to 30 s (projectBridge.js:5).
- Trigger: a single slow or failed poll (service busy hashing or archiving, the 30 s timeout, a
  browser connection limit), exactly the case where the service is under load.
- MEASURED unit cost: each reconnect attempt that succeeds returns 64.3 MB; ESTIMATED impact: up to
  5 overlapping 31.8 MB status requests while the service is slow, then a UI flip to cloud-only
  data and a 64 MB reload. This is the "transient failure treated as definitive" pattern.
- Fix: chain polls with `setTimeout` after completion (never overlap), require 3 consecutive
  failures before `connected = false`, and reconnect with a tiny `ping` action, then fetch
  summaries (F6).

### F8. MEDIUM. Local image thumbnails load eagerly and stream the original file into a 44 px cell
- Code: `AssetsWorkspaceView.jsx:40-49` `LocalThumbnail` posts `preview-url` on mount, no
  visibility gate; used by `renderThumbnail` 250 for every row, tile, rail miniature and cover;
  `AssetsService.mjs:1386-1418` `handlePreview` streams the original bytes.
- Trigger: icons or gallery view, Images filter, rail with 15 project covers.
- MEASURED: vegetation holds 2,811 local images, median 0.71 MB, p90 6.40 MB, max 30.4 MB,
  6.77 GB total; one page of 100 images (Images filter, name order) = 78.3 MB to download and decode
  for 44 to 280 px thumbnails, plus 100 eager POSTs competing with the 32 MB polls.
- Fix: gate with the existing `useInView` (src/media/useImageThumb.js, already used by TextThumb)
  and add `size` to the preview endpoint, served from a thumbnail cache keyed by sha256
  (`sips -Z 256` or the same AVIF CRF 25 pipeline), so each tile costs tens of KB.

### F9. MEDIUM. The 10-second conversation poll re-renders the whole workspace even when nothing changed
- Code: `AssetsWorkspaceView.jsx:99-111` always `setConversations(result.conversations)` (new
  array); `readConversation` 98 also maps the array; `ConversationView.jsx:37` polls every 10 s and
  `ConversationMessage` 16 re-runs `safeMarkedParse` on every message each render; ProjectWorkspace
  is not memoized and receives inline callbacks, so the rail re-sorts 572 items with `Date.parse`
  (118) and FileFilters/columns recompute.
- MEASURED: 1,002,999 bytes per poll (572 conversations, 1,753 B each with localPath,
  originalPaths, transcriptPaths), cold catalog scan 612 ms; re-render costs measured in F3/F10.
  The poll runs even when the Conversations shelf is closed.
- Fix: poll only while the conversation shelf or a conversation is visible; skip `setState` when
  `result.checkedAt` and the item count/signatures are unchanged; trim paths from the list (they
  are only needed in the reader); memoize message HTML with `useMemo` on `message.text`.

### F10. LOW. Columns view recomputes its folder tree from all files on every render
- Code: `src/components/assets/FilePresentations.jsx:33-50`, receiving `visible` (all 18,423) from
  `ProjectWorkspace.jsx:348`; `pathParts` re-splits each path several times per render.
- MEASURED: 39.0 ms per render at trail depth 4 (inline `node -e` over the vegetation copy);
  paid on every selection click, every status poll and every conversation poll.
- Fix: `useMemo` a prefix tree (`Map<prefix, entries>`) keyed on `files`, and compute `pathParts`
  once per file.

### F11. LOW. Each refresh rebuilds the 154,000-path index array, invalidating every consumer
- Code: `src/search/searchIndexClient.js:107-123`, `applyLocalOverlay` creates a new Set and a new
  `paths` array on every `loadSearchIndex()`, called by `refresh()` (AssetsWorkspaceView.jsx:121).
- MEASURED: 12.8 ms per rebuild at 154,000 paths; the new reference re-triggers F4 (about 67 ms)
  and, per the comment at searchIndexClient.js:218-226, forces the global search to renormalize
  the whole index (NFD) on its next keystroke. That last cost is ESTIMATED, not measured here.
- Fix: return the previous `rec.paths` when `localAdds`/`localRemoves` are empty or unchanged
  since the last overlay (keep a version counter).

## Priority order (7 October 2026)

F1 + F2 (light status and job polling) remove almost all bandwidth; F3a (hoisted collator) is a
one-line change worth about 316 ms per poll and per keystroke; F6 stops a read-only page from
writing 31 MB state files; F7 then F8.
